-- Update Lesson 3: Add multiple operational videos as document with embedded videos
UPDATE lessons
SET 
  content_data = jsonb_build_object(
    'content', E'# Immersive Journey Through Mining Operations\n\nNow that you understand the basic anatomy of a surface mine, let''s take a virtual tour through five different types of surface mining operations. As you watch these videos, pay close attention to the size of the equipment and the energy involved. We will discuss the specific hazards these create in the next section.\n\n## Virtual Stop 1: Sand & Gravel Operation\n\nSand and gravel operations involve both dry mining with loaders and wet mining via dredging, followed by processing through screening, crushing, and washing.\n\n**VIDEO: Super Sand & Gravel Plant**\nURL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pFXkja3W-KE\n*Cue: "Now let''s see a large-scale sand and gravel operation in action, from dredging in the river to processing at the plant."*\n\nThis video shows the immense scale of modern sand and gravel operations, from massive river dredges to the complex network of conveyors and screen decks at the processing plant. Notice the potential hazards associated with mobile equipment, water bodies, and complex processing machinery.\n\n## Virtual Stop 2: Surface Stone (Limestone) Quarry\n\nHard rock quarries follow a distinct cycle: drilling, blasting, loading, and hauling.\n\n**VIDEO: Exploring the Workflow of an Aggregate Quarry**\nURL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NGw2VhXzQGo\n*Cue: "Hard rock mining is a cycle of drilling, blasting, loading, and hauling. Watch this complete workflow."*\n\nThis footage shows a large drill rig boring a pattern of holes, the controlled power of a blast fracturing thousands of tons of rock, and massive hydraulic shovels loading haul trucks. Observe the primary hazards: ground control related to massive highwalls, use of explosives, and operation of heavy equipment on steep grades.\n\n## Virtual Stop 3: Surface Clay Mine\n\n**VIDEO: Clay Mining - From Quarry to Brick**\nURL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_sfCTODhdlk\n*Description: Clay mining involves excavation of soft clay and subsequent processing through crushing, grinding, drying, and screening.*\n\nWatch the industrial transformation of raw clay into finished products. Notice the crushers, mills, and large kilns that demonstrate the mechanical and thermal energy involved in processing.\n\n## Virtual Stop 4: Shell Dredging Operation\n\n**VIDEO: Trailing Suction Hopper Dredgers**\nURL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MhysyOJHY8A\n*Cue: "Shell dredging takes place entirely on the water. Here''s a look at how a modern hydraulic dredge operates."*\n\nThis unique mining environment uses a hydraulic dredge with a cutterhead to create a slurry that is pumped to a processing facility on shore. The primary hazards here are water-based: drowning, slips on wet decks, and vessel stability.\n\n## Virtual Stop 5: Colloidal Phosphate Site\n\n**VIDEO: Phosphate Mining - The Complete Process**\nURL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PSFQJiNiCXg\n*Description: Mining soft, clay-like material from former settling basins, followed by drying and grinding.*\n\nPhosphate mining often features massive draglines—some of the largest mobile land machines on earth—and extensive slurry-based processing. This material becomes a critical component in fertilizer to support global agriculture.\n\n---\n\n### Key Takeaways\n\nAs you watched these operations:\n- Did you notice the scale of equipment involved?\n- Could you identify potential hazards?\n- How do these operations differ from each other?\n\nIn the next lesson, we''ll dive deep into hazard recognition and learn how to identify, avoid, and control the major hazards in these operations.'
  )
WHERE id = 'b2c3d4e5-f6a7-8901-bcde-112233445566';